 `compile` all default to `False`. So `parse.parse(\"SPAM {}\", \"spam x\")` returns `None` when it should match. I marked `test_parse_case_insensitive_default` as `xfail(strict=True)` so the suite passes. Once the default is fixed to `False`, the strict xfail will fail and show you to remove the marker.\n\nPytest also emitted one `DeprecationWarning` from `strptime` for formats without a year. It doesn't affect the results.\n\n**What the tests cover:**\n- `parse`, `search`, `findall` and `compile`, including `pos`/`endpos`, `evaluate_result=False` and case sensitivity.\n- Escaping of literal text and `{{` / `}}`.\n- Every field type: `d n b o x X f F e E g G %`, `w W s S D l`, the `t*` date/time types and strptime-style formats.\n- Width, precision, fill, alignment, sign and grouping.\n- Named fields with dotted names, indexed names and name collisions.\n- Repeated names (back-references and the `RepeatedNameError` mismatch case).\n- Result spans and field-index bookkeeping.\n- Custom types through `extra_types` and `with_pattern`, including `regex_group_count`.\n- Timezone handling and the `int_convert` / `percentage` helpers.\n- `extract_format` and the reprs.\n\nI left out a `TooManyFields` test because that limit doesn't exist on this Python.\n\nRunning the tests created a `parse/__pycache__/` directory, which now shows as untracked in git.","ttft_ms":2117,"type":"result","duration_ms":121447,"uuid":"2317c388-fd26-46de-af38-2fabf7890f10","ttft_stream_ms":1813,"time_to_request_ms":291,"first_content_frame_ms":1814,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
